I peeked at the latest version of PatchHack
http://patchhack.sourceforge.net/, the file patchhack-nh340-1.diff from
2002. Since then, we have had a new NetHack version 3.4.3. You can
download a binary of NetHack 3.4.3 from
http://www.nethack.org/v343/downloads.html

To play with patches, you *need* a compiler. You could ask someone to
make a binary for you, but everyone seems to want to configure their
patches differently or has a different operating system. There are free
compilers and patch programs that you can download.

For BSD (including Mac OS X) you could try instructions that I wrote
for StrategyWiki:
* http://strategywiki.org/wiki/NetHack/Building#Unix

For Linux and Windows, try Wikihack:
* http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Compiling
* http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Patching

You might also want to look at NAO http://alt.org/nethack that is a
telnet server with 3.4.3 and some nice interface patches. NAO is why I
never need NetHack binaries except for wizard mode.

